---
<section class="section techbook-section techbook-plan" id="plan" aria-labelledby="plan-title">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">THE PLAN</p>
    <h2 id="plan-title">TechBook — 12-Step AI Engineering Build Plan</h2>
    <div class="body-copy techbook-plan-intro">
      <p><strong>Objective:</strong> Build and deploy TechBook, an AI-powered technical service booking application, while implementing all 12 modern AI engineering concepts under Define • Design • Deliver • Defend.</p>
      <p>We will use GitHub Copilot in VS Code for development, OpenAI for the application's reasoning, Java/Spring Boot, React, PostgreSQL and an MCP server. Deployment will be on Hostinger using Docker, independently of your personal website.</p>
      <p>Each step will have a clear deliverable and completion criterion. We move forward when the deliverable is acceptable, not simply when AI says the work is finished.</p>
    </div>
    {phases.map((phase) => (
      <section class="plan-phase" aria-labelledby={`phase-${phase.name.toLowerCase()}`}>
        <h3 id={`phase-${phase.name.toLowerCase()}`}>{phase.name} <span>— {phase.subtitle}</span></h3>
        <div class="plan-steps">
          {phase.steps.map((step) => (
            <details class="plan-step">
              <summary><span class="plan-number">{step.number}</span><span>{step.title}</span></summary>
              <div class="plan-step-content">
                {step.description.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
                <h4>Deliverables</h4>
                <ul>{step.deliverables.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}</ul>
                <p class="plan-completion"><strong>Complete when:</strong> {step.complete}</p>
              </div>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}
    <section class="plan-outcomes" aria-labelledby="plan-outcomes-title">
      <h3 id="plan-outcomes-title">What we'll have at the end</h3>
      <div class="plan-outcome-grid">
        <div><h4>Defined</h4><p>Approved requirements, specifications, acceptance criteria and agent context.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Designed</h4><p>Documented architecture, MCP contracts and agent orchestration.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Delivered</h4><p>A functioning AI-powered technical booking system built using agentic coding practices.</p></div>
        <div><h4>Defended</h4><p>Independent assurance, automated testing, traceability and continuous monitoring.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="plan-sequencing" aria-labelledby="plan-sequencing-title">
      <h3 id="plan-sequencing-title">A practical point about sequencing</h3>
      <div class="body-copy">
        <p>Although the plan has 12 steps, I would not defer all testing until Steps 10–12. Acceptance criteria begin in Step 2, automated testing starts with the first code in Step 7, and assurance evolves as we build.</p>
        <p>Likewise, the agent roles are introduced when needed rather than creating a large agent infrastructure upfront.</p>
        <p>My recommendation: Treat each step as a small, reviewable engineering milestone. We finish with a working TechBook application and, equally importantly, a documented approach to AI-native enterprise software engineering that we can explain, challenge and develop further through the LAB.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>
